WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Good morning John!

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.380
oh yeah yeah look at

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.640
that tire

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.480
That one's pretty squishy.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.460
Is it okay to

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:11.594
touch random people's bikes?

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:12.986
You want to hear a funny story?

00:00:12.986 --> 00:00:13.486
I left my computer on an airplane

00:00:13.929 --> 00:00:16.150
so I'm having other people

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.260
edit this vlog for me.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.400
Here's the plan:  I put this footage

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.400
on the Internet. People on the

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.789
internet then take that footage

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:23.619
everybody makes their own video with it

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:25.240
and then we vote on which one goes on

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.529
the vlogbrothers channel and we do this all

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:27.553
within like 24 hours.

00:00:27.553 --> 00:00:28.480
So amsterdam things I need

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.919
I need to find. I need to

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.780
see like rowhouse, bicyclers

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.420
which shouldn't be hard,

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.460
a canal.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:35.440
I found bicyclers.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.300
(music) Sometimes the world looks perfect.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.560
nothing to rearrange

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.020
sometimes you

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.040
just get a feeling

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.100
like you need some kind of change

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.220
(Hank talking)

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.200
This is a questionable strategy I've made

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.399
which is to just to start walking and

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:53.739
see if I find something good.

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:54.839
I am immediately lost.

00:00:54.839 --> 00:00:56.140
This city is not on a grid

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.949
and also my phone doesn't a hundred

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:01.989
percent work like I can call and text

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:04.239
but it cannot use maps. There's no data.

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:05.710
So to get real honest, I'm gonna have to work

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.840
it out the old-fashioned way

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.960
uhh, which I have

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.320
completely forgotten how to do.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.200
I mean even the littering is neat.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.920
They just left it there, right side up.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.500
What is a "chocomouth"? It smells like chocolate

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.260
Is it like "Yoo-hoo"?  I was going to

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.610
read the label but it's all in Dutch.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.380
Sometimes you see things on the

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.550
ground you don't know what they are and

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.596
Have to find out.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.300
Oh! It's like a little light,

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.200
the tiniest, cheapest bike light

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.340
you could possibly imagine.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.900
You know. I'm keeping it.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.340
I mean...

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.240
presented without comment.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.300
Hey Pigeon, there's a whole tortilla

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.500
like on a windowsill right over there.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:45.720
Whole tortilla. You could feed your entire

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:46.880
family for a month.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.189
A whole tortilla.

00:01:48.189 --> 00:01:50.300
Stop walking away from me! I'm trying to help!

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.540
Found row houses

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.220
with the little hooks that they used to get stuff up

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.860
because you can't carry 'em up

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.240
cuz they're too skinny.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.440
All that's left is a canal.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.400
I have to find a canal

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.560
I just saw a fourth Amsterdam thing:

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.740
2 people just smoked pot on the street,

00:02:04.742 --> 00:02:07.299
which of course is normal here. I think this is a

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.080
wedding cake made out of diapers.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.440
That's...I... you... yep, yep

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.100
I definitely am going the wrong direction.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.520
But wait, but just ahead of the

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.470
highway, just in front of it

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.840
I think... What is it?

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.840
It's a canal. It's a big one!

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.700
Ooo a moorhen! Can you see it?

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.000
Oh, it just disappeared. Bye, Moorhen!

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.220
Come back! I'm making a video.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.720
Hello? It was like 'I don't...

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.520
we don't like to be on vid-'  There it is. Hey!

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.250
John, the Dutch people think that I'm weird

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.660
but that's okay.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.640
I think the dutch people are weird.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:37.940
You know this might not be a canal.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.280
This might be a river.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.709
It might be the river Amstel, I feel like,

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:43.500
Maybe. Maybe not. I don't know!

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.100
I have come to the definitive conclusion that I'm

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.080
not in the canal-y part of Amsterdam.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.360
ok, John, I'm 90% sure this is the

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.700
same canal I was at before.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.420
But I am now a hundred percent sure

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.800
that it is, in fact, a canal.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:56.590
Which means I found all the

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:57.900
things that I was looking for.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.120
So now I have to try and find my

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.340
way back to where I was.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.740
I don't even know what my hotel looks like.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.010
This is the street where they keep all

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.500
the cars in Amsterdam.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.980
Every single Amsterdam car

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.900
is here right now.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.500
The pigeon didn't listen to me.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.000
I see these bikes and- I just- I think

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.260
many of them must have just been here

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.520
for centuries

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.200
I feel like they're

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.340
intentionally leaving old bikes just so

00:03:20.349 --> 00:03:22.060
it looks like there are a lot of bikers.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.840
It's gotta be a lot of these bikes not in use.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.080
Like this. This one!

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.980
This is just still here right?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:30.540
like somebody

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:31.940
has left it there.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.200
or do they? Yeah, yeah, look at that tire

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.680
I'm very glad to finally be in this city

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.740
which I've wanted to go to for a long time,

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.520
and to be here for VidCon Europe

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.720
which is going to be a ball.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:44.520
I would like to thank

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.800
this person

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.820
for editing this video.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.260
There's a lot of other versions,

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.340
hopefully, of this video,

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.540
edited by other people.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.860
I encourage you, John,

00:03:52.862 --> 00:03:53.390
and also

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:54.799
anyone else to go look at those videos.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.260
Thanks to all the people who helped me with this.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.320
Thanks John.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.620
And I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:03:59.400
(stranger in car) bye.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.740
(Hank) bye!

